@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `vn13-nouns`
IMPORT `vn13-fixtures`
IMPORT `vn13-art01-02-definitions`
IMPORT `vn13-art09-10-premiums`
IMPORT `vn13-art11-12-funds`
IMPORT `vn13-art13-charges`
IMPORT `vn13-annex1-funds`
IMPORT `vn13-annex2-procedures`

-- Tests for the mechanics: premiums and units (Article 9), the funds (11, 12), the charges
-- (13) and the Annexes. Every expected value was worked by hand from the text, the working
-- beside it; the two tables' row tests are generated from the source by tools/gen_tables.py.
-- A failing assertion is a finding, never a value to edit.

§ `Tests — mechanics`

§§ `Article 9.1 and 9.2 — premiums buy units`

-- 9.1: after the first premium, unpaid on or before the due date counts as not paid.
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 9.1 —` (`the half-yearly premium due on 10 July 2026, paid` (JUST (YMD 2026 7 10))) `counts as not paid, a premium holiday applying:` FALSE)
#ASSERT `Article 9.1 —` (`the half-yearly premium due on 10 July 2026, paid` (JUST (YMD 2026 7 11))) `counts as not paid, a premium holiday applying:` FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 9.1 —` (`the half-yearly premium due on 10 July 2026, paid` NOTHING) `counts as not paid, a premium holiday applying:` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 9.1 —` (`the half-yearly premium due on 10 July 2026, paid` NOTHING) `counts as not paid, a premium holiday applying:` TRUE)

-- The first annual instalment of 20,000,000 at the 90% initial charge leaves 2,000,000;
-- half to each fund. Offer prices: Growth 9,500 / 0.95 = 10,000; Balanced 19,000 / 0.95
-- = 20,000. Units: 1,000,000 / 10,000 = 100 and 1,000,000 / 20,000 = 50.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      a IS A NUMBER
      r IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A regular basic premium instalment`
`annual instalment` n `of` a `at an initial charge of` r MEANS
    `A regular basic premium instalment` WITH
        `instalment number`   IS n
        `frequency`           IS `annual premiums`
        `amount`              IS a
        `initial charge rate` IS r

#ASSERT map (GIVEN c YIELD c's `units added`) (`Article 9.1 — the units bought with` (`annual instalment` 1 `of` 20_000_000 `at an initial charge of` 0.9) `allocated by` `half Growth, half Balanced` `at the offer prices of` `the funds on 13 March 2030` `with a spread of` (5%)) EQUALS LIST 100, 50
-- The fourth instalment at 0%: 20,000,000, so 1,000 and 500 units.
#ASSERT map (GIVEN c YIELD c's `units added`) (`Article 9.1 — the units bought with` (`annual instalment` 4 `of` 20_000_000 `at an initial charge of` 0) `allocated by` `half Growth, half Balanced` `at the offer prices of` `the funds on 13 March 2030` `with a spread of` (5%)) EQUALS LIST 1_000, 500
-- A top-up of 10,000,000, no initial charge: 500 and 250 units.
#ASSERT map (GIVEN c YIELD c's `units added`) (`Article 9.2 — the units bought with` (`A top-up premium` WITH `date paid` IS YMD 2030 3 12, `amount` IS 10_000_000, `initial charge rate` IS 0) `allocated by` `half Growth, half Balanced` `at the offer prices of` `the funds on 13 March 2030` `with a spread of` (5%)) EQUALS LIST 500, 250
-- A fund with no valuation that day: refused.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the bid price of` (`a fund established later under Article 11.4` "Fund X") `among` `the funds on 13 March 2030` BECAUSE "no valuation of that fund on the Valuation Date was supplied"

§§ `Article 9.3 — premium holiday`

-- From the second policy year (10 January 2027), while in force.
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 9.3 — a premium holiday may be asked for on` (YMD 2027 1 9) `, the contract being effective from` (YMD 2026 1 10) `and in force:` TRUE)
#ASSERT `Article 9.3 — a premium holiday may be asked for on` (YMD 2027 1 10) `, the contract being effective from` (YMD 2026 1 10) `and in force:` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 9.3 — a premium holiday may be asked for on` (YMD 2027 1 10) `, the contract being effective from` (YMD 2026 1 10) `and in force:` FALSE)
-- Delay without notice: a premium due 10 July 2026 (first year): the riders end on
-- 9 September 2026, the day after the 60 days. A premium due in the second year: no rule.
#ASSERT `Article 9.3 — the day the riders end, a premium due on` (YMD 2026 7 10) `being delayed without notice, for a contract effective on` (YMD 2026 1 10) EQUALS YMD 2026 9 9
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 9.3 — the day the riders end, a premium due on` (YMD 2027 7 10) `being delayed without notice, for a contract effective on` (YMD 2026 1 10) BECAUSE "from the second policy year a delay in premiums opens no grace period, so Article 9.3 does not say when the riders end"
-- A notified holiday, risk premium 100,000, policy fee 50,000, riders 80,000 (230,000):
#ASSERT `Article 9.3 — the contract at a monthly deduction during a notified premium holiday, given` (`an account with a surrender value of` 1_000_000) EQUALS `the deductions are met, riders included`
#ASSERT `Article 9.3 — the contract at a monthly deduction during a notified premium holiday, given` (`an account with a surrender value of` 230_000) EQUALS `the deductions are met, riders included`
#ASSERT `Article 9.3 — the contract at a monthly deduction during a notified premium holiday, given` (`an account with a surrender value of` 229_999) EQUALS `the riders end, and the surrender value meets only the risk premium and policy fee`
#ASSERT `Article 9.3 — the contract at a monthly deduction during a notified premium holiday, given` (`an account with a surrender value of` 150_000) EQUALS `the riders end, and the surrender value meets only the risk premium and policy fee`
#ASSERT `Article 9.3 — the contract at a monthly deduction during a notified premium holiday, given` (`an account with a surrender value of` 149_999) EQUALS `the grace period of Article 9.4 begins`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 9.3 does not say how the premium after a holiday is calculated` BECAUSE "Article 9.3 does not say how the premium after a holiday is calculated"

§§ `Article 9.4 — grace and lapse`

-- First policy year, half-yearly premium due 10 July 2026. 60 days later is 8 September.
#ASSERT `the last day of the grace period of a premium due on` (YMD 2026 7 10) EQUALS YMD 2026 9 8
#ASSERT `Article 9.4 — what follows from` (`the half-yearly premium due on 10 July 2026, paid` (JUST (YMD 2026 7 10))) `, for a contract effective on` (YMD 2026 1 10) EQUALS `paid on or before the due date`
#ASSERT `Article 9.4 — what follows from` (`the half-yearly premium due on 10 July 2026, paid` (JUST (YMD 2026 9 8))) `, for a contract effective on` (YMD 2026 1 10) EQUALS `paid within the grace period`
#ASSERT `Article 9.4 — what follows from` (`the half-yearly premium due on 10 July 2026, paid` (JUST (YMD 2026 9 9))) `, for a contract effective on` (YMD 2026 1 10) EQUALS `the contract lapses on` (YMD 2026 9 9)
#ASSERT `Article 9.4 — what follows from` (`the half-yearly premium due on 10 July 2026, paid` NOTHING) `, for a contract effective on` (YMD 2026 1 10) EQUALS `the contract lapses on` (YMD 2026 9 9)
-- Due in the second policy year: no grace period from the missed premium itself.
#ASSERT `Article 9.4 — what follows from` (`A regular premium falling due` WITH `due date` IS YMD 2027 1 10, `date paid` IS NOTHING) `, for a contract effective on` (YMD 2026 1 10) EQUALS `no grace period, the premium falling due after the first policy year`
-- The surrender value on a first-year lapse on 9 September 2026: the next valuation.
#ASSERT `Article 9.4 — the surrender value paid on a first-year lapse on` (YMD 2026 9 9) `, among` (LIST (`a valuation on` (YMD 2026 9 9) `: Growth` 100 `at` 9_000 `, Balanced` 50 `at` 10_000 `, premium debt` 0), (`a valuation on` (YMD 2026 9 16) `: Growth` 100 `at` 9_500 `, Balanced` 50 `at` 10_000 `, premium debt` 0)) EQUALS 1_450_000
-- As a duty: paid on day 60, fulfilled; nothing by day 61, the Company must pay the
-- surrender value; it does, fulfilled.
#TRACE `Article 9.4 — the first-year premium and its grace period` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Policyholder` DOES `pay the regular basic premium` AT 60
#TRACE `Article 9.4 — the first-year premium and its grace period` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 61)
#TRACE `Article 9.4 — the first-year premium and its grace period` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 61)
    PARTY `the Company` DOES `pay the surrender value` AT 70
-- From the second policy year: risk premium 100,000 + policy fee 50,000.
#ASSERT `Article 9.4 — a grace period begins at a monthly deduction on` (YMD 2028 3 10) `, for a contract effective on` (YMD 2026 1 10) `, given` (`an account with a surrender value of` 149_999)
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 9.4 — a grace period begins at a monthly deduction on` (YMD 2028 3 10) `, for a contract effective on` (YMD 2026 1 10) `, given` (`an account with a surrender value of` 150_000))
-- In the first policy year a shortfall is not provided for; no shortfall, no grace period.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 9.4 — a grace period begins at a monthly deduction on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `, for a contract effective on` (YMD 2026 1 10) `, given` (`an account with a surrender value of` 149_999) BECAUSE "Article 9.4 does not say what follows when the surrender value cannot meet a monthly deduction in the first policy year"
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 9.4 — a grace period begins at a monthly deduction on` (YMD 2026 6 10) `, for a contract effective on` (YMD 2026 1 10) `, given` (`an account with a surrender value of` 150_000))
-- A grace period that began 10 March 2028 ends the contract on 10 May 2028 (61 days on).
#ASSERT `Article 9.4 — the end of a grace period that began on` (YMD 2028 3 10) `, a sufficient payment being received:` FALSE EQUALS `the contract ends without surrender value on` (YMD 2028 5 10)
#ASSERT `Article 9.4 — the end of a grace period that began on` (YMD 2028 3 10) `, a sufficient payment being received:` TRUE EQUALS `the contract continues, a sufficient payment having been received`
#ASSERT `Article 9.4 — a benefit of` 757_300_000 `paid in a grace period, less unpaid charges of` 150_000 EQUALS 757_150_000

§§ `Article 9.5 — reinstatement`

GIVEN `the request date` IS A DATE
      `alive`            IS A BOOLEAN
      `surrendered`      IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A reinstatement request`
`a reinstatement request on` `the request date` `, alive` `alive` `, surrendered` `surrendered` MEANS
    `A reinstatement request` WITH
        `lapse date`                                       IS YMD 2026 9 9
        `request date`                                     IS `the request date`
        `the Life Insured alive on the request date`       IS `alive`
        `surrendered for its surrender value`              IS `surrendered`
        `request in writing`                               IS TRUE
        `evidence of insurability accepted by the Company` IS TRUE
        `the amount the Company set has been paid`         IS TRUE

-- Lapsed 9 September 2026: two years end on 9 September 2028.
#ASSERT `Article 9.5 — the contract may be reinstated on` (`a reinstatement request on` (YMD 2028 9 9) `, alive` TRUE `, surrendered` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 9.5 — the contract may be reinstated on` (`a reinstatement request on` (YMD 2028 9 10) `, alive` TRUE `, surrendered` FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 9.5 — the contract may be reinstated on` (`a reinstatement request on` (YMD 2027 1 1) `, alive` FALSE `, surrendered` FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 9.5 — the contract may be reinstated on` (`a reinstatement request on` (YMD 2027 1 1) `, alive` TRUE `, surrendered` TRUE))

§§ `Article 10`

#ASSERT `Article 10 — a payment complies, being in` `Vietnamese dong`
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 10 — a payment complies, being in` `another currency`)

§§ `Article 11.2 — prices and valuation`

-- Bid: 1,000,000,000 / 100,000 units = 10,000. Offer at 5%: 10,000 / 0.95 = 200,000 / 19,
-- about 10,526.32; times 0.95 it is the bid again.
#ASSERT `Article 11.2 — the bid price of a unit of` (`A fund on a valuation date` WITH `fund` IS `the Growth Fund`, `valuation date` IS YMD 2030 3 6, `net asset value` IS 1_000_000_000, `units in issue` IS 100_000) EQUALS 10_000
#ASSERT `Article 11.2 — the offer price for a bid price of` 10_000 `and a spread of` (5%) EQUALS 200_000 DIVIDED BY 19
#ASSERT `Article 11.2 — the offer price for a bid price of` 10_000 `and a spread of` (5%) TIMES 0.95 EQUALS 10_000
-- At least weekly: 7 days apart is enough, 8 is not.
#ASSERT `Article 11.2 — the funds are valued at least once a week, on` (LIST (YMD 2030 3 6), (YMD 2030 3 13), (YMD 2030 3 20))
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 11.2 — the funds are valued at least once a week, on` (LIST (YMD 2030 3 6), (YMD 2030 3 14)))

§§ `Article 11.3 — units`

-- 1,000 units, plus 100 bought, less 50 switched out, less 10 for charges: 1,040.
#ASSERT `Article 11.3 — the units after` 1_000 `and` (LIST (`A change in units` WITH `fund` IS `the Growth Fund`, `reason` IS `allocation of a regular basic premium or a top-up premium`, `units added` IS 100), (`A change in units` WITH `fund` IS `the Growth Fund`, `reason` IS `a fund switch`, `units added` IS 0 MINUS 50), (`A change in units` WITH `fund` IS `the Growth Fund`, `reason` IS `the risk premium, the monthly policy fee or another fund charge`, `units added` IS 0 MINUS 10)) EQUALS 1_040
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 11.3 — the units after` 1_000 `and` (LIST (`A change in units` WITH `fund` IS `the Growth Fund`, `reason` IS `a reason Article 11.3 does not list`, `units added` IS 0 MINUS 10)) BECAUSE "Article 11.3 does not allow a change in units for that reason"

§§ `Article 11.4 and 11.7 — notice before a measure`

-- Notice on 1 March 2030: a closure may apply on 4 March, not on 3 March.
#ASSERT `Article 11.4 and 11.7 —` `closing or renaming a fund under Article 11.4` `may be applied, with notice given on` (JUST (YMD 2030 3 1)) `, on` (YMD 2030 3 4)
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 11.4 and 11.7 —` `closing or renaming a fund under Article 11.4` `may be applied, with notice given on` (JUST (YMD 2030 3 1)) `, on` (YMD 2030 3 3))
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 11.4 and 11.7 —` `renaming a fund` `may be applied, with notice given on` NOTHING `, on` (YMD 2030 3 3))
-- Suspending valuation (11.7 d) needs no notice.
#ASSERT `Article 11.4 and 11.7 —` `suspending valuation and transactions while the exchange is suspended` `may be applied, with notice given on` NOTHING `, on` (YMD 2030 3 3)
-- A closed fund's units: as asked; failing a request, Annex 2 has no procedure.
#ASSERT `Article 11.4 — what becomes of the units of a closed fund, given` TRUE EQUALS "bought back, or moved to the fund the Company names, as the Policyholder asked"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 11.4 — what becomes of the units of a closed fund, given` FALSE BECAUSE "Article 11.4 points to an Annex 2 procedure for a closed fund's units, and Annex 2 has none"

§§ `Article 11.5, 11.6, 11.8, 11.9 and Article 12`

-- Redeeming 100 Growth units on a transaction effective Sunday 10 March 2030: the bid on
-- 13 March is 16,000, so 1,600,000.
#ASSERT `Article 11.5 — the amount withdrawn by redeeming` 100 `units of` `the Growth Fund` `on a transaction effective` (YMD 2030 3 10) `, among` `the valuations of March 2030` EQUALS 1_600_000
-- Switching 1,020,000 into a fund whose bid is 10,200 buys 100 units.
#ASSERT `Article 11.6 — the units bought by switching in` 1_020_000 `at a bid price of` 10_200 EQUALS 100
-- 11.8: received 19,000,000 of 20,000,000: may be refused; in full: not.
#ASSERT `Article 11.8 — the Company may refuse a premium of` 20_000_000 `when it has received` 19_000_000
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 11.8 — the Company may refuse a premium of` 20_000_000 `when it has received` 20_000_000)
#ASSERT `Article 11.8 — a refund of` 1 `of a refused premium of` 19_000_000 `is one the Article allows`
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 11.8 — a refund of` 19_000_001 `of a refused premium of` 19_000_000 `is one the Article allows`)
-- 11.9: net assets 1,000,000,000, so the daily cap is 100,000,000. Requests of 50,000,000
-- and of exactly 100,000,000 are met in full; of 200,000,000, half each, and a request of
-- 40,000,000 carries 20,000,000 to the next Valuation Date.
#ASSERT `Article 11.9 — the share of each request met, for a fund with net assets of` 1_000_000_000 `and requests of` 50_000_000 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `Article 11.9 — the share of each request met, for a fund with net assets of` 1_000_000_000 `and requests of` 100_000_000 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `Article 11.9 — the share of each request met, for a fund with net assets of` 1_000_000_000 `and requests of` 200_000_000 EQUALS 0.5
#ASSERT `Article 11.9 — the part of a request of` 40_000_000 `carried to the next Valuation Date, for a fund with net assets of` 1_000_000_000 `and requests of` 200_000_000 EQUALS 20_000_000
-- Article 12: a surrender received Sunday 10 March 2030 is paid at 13 March, 209,000,000;
-- one received on Wednesday 13 March (itself a Valuation Date) at 20 March, 220,000,000.
#ASSERT `Article 12 — the surrender payment for a request received on` (YMD 2030 3 10) `, among` `the valuations of March 2030` EQUALS 209_000_000
#ASSERT `Article 12 — the surrender payment for a request received on` (YMD 2030 3 13) `, among` `the valuations of March 2030` EQUALS 220_000_000
#ASSERT `Article 12 — the Policyholder may surrender the contract, it being in force:` TRUE `; requested in writing on the form:` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 12 — the Policyholder may surrender the contract, it being in force:` TRUE `; requested in writing on the form:` FALSE)

§§ `Article 13 — charges`

-- A change notified 1 January 2026 may apply from 1 April 2026, not 31 March; only if
-- agreed in writing and not above the maximum.
GIVEN `the date applied` IS A DATE
      `agreed`           IS A BOOLEAN
      `the new level`    IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A change in a charge`
`a charge change applied on` `the date applied` `, agreed` `agreed` `, to` `the new level` MEANS
    `A change in a charge` WITH
        `date of the written notice`            IS YMD 2026 1 1
        `date the new charge applies`           IS `the date applied`
        `agreed in writing by the Policyholder` IS `agreed`
        `new level`                             IS `the new level`
        `guaranteed maximum`                    IS 57_500

#ASSERT `Article 13 — the changed charge may apply` (`a charge change applied on` (YMD 2026 4 1) `, agreed` TRUE `, to` 57_500)
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 13 — the changed charge may apply` (`a charge change applied on` (YMD 2026 3 31) `, agreed` TRUE `, to` 57_500))
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 13 — the changed charge may apply` (`a charge change applied on` (YMD 2026 4 1) `, agreed` FALSE `, to` 57_500))
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 13 — the changed charge may apply` (`a charge change applied on` (YMD 2026 4 1) `, agreed` TRUE `, to` 57_501))

-- 13.1: 90% of 20,000,000 is 18,000,000; the allocated premium is 2,000,000.
#ASSERT `Article 13.1 — the initial charge on a premium of` 20_000_000 `at a rate of` (90%) EQUALS 18_000_000
#ASSERT `the allocated basic premium of` (`annual instalment` 1 `of` 20_000_000 `at an initial charge of` 0.9) EQUALS 2_000_000
#ASSERT `the allocated top-up premium of` (`A top-up premium` WITH `date paid` IS YMD 2030 3 12, `amount` IS 10_000_000, `initial charge rate` IS 0) EQUALS 10_000_000
-- 13.3: 500,000,000 at 0.0002 a month is 100,000. 13.6: plus the 50,000 fee, 150,000.
#ASSERT `Article 13.3 — the risk premium on a sum assured of` 500_000_000 `at a rate of` 0.0002 EQUALS 100_000
#ASSERT `Article 13.6 — the monthly deduction on a sum assured of` 500_000_000 `under` `the charges` EQUALS 150_000
-- 13.6 sharing: Growth 150,000,000 of 200,000,000 bears 112,500, at 15,000 = 7.5 units;
-- Balanced 37,500 at 10,000 = 3.75 units. The account falls by exactly 150,000.
GIVETH A LIST OF `A holding in a fund`
`the holdings of 6 March 2030` MEANS
    LIST (`A holding in a fund` WITH `fund` IS `the Growth Fund`,   `units held` IS 10_000, `bid price` IS 15_000),
         (`A holding in a fund` WITH `fund` IS `the Balanced Fund`, `units held` IS 5_000,  `bid price` IS 10_000)

#ASSERT map (GIVEN h YIELD h's `units held`) (`Article 13.6 — the holdings after a deduction of` 150_000 `from` `the holdings of 6 March 2030`) EQUALS LIST 9_992.5, 4_996.25
#ASSERT `the total account value of` (`Article 13.6 — the holdings after a deduction of` 150_000 `from` `the holdings of 6 March 2030`) EQUALS 199_850_000
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 13.6 — the units cancelled from` (`A holding in a fund` WITH `fund` IS `the Growth Fund`, `units held` IS 0, `bid price` IS 15_000) `for a deduction of` 150_000 `shared across` (LIST (`A holding in a fund` WITH `fund` IS `the Growth Fund`, `units held` IS 0, `bid price` IS 15_000)) BECAUSE "an account with no value cannot share a monthly deduction; Article 9.3 and 9.4 govern"
-- 13.5: 10,000,000 withdrawn, fee 200,000, 9,800,000 paid out.
#ASSERT `Article 13.5 — what is paid out of a withdrawal of` 10_000_000 `with a fee of` 200_000 EQUALS 9_800_000
-- 13.8 and 13.9 h: 2.5% a year of 200,000,000 is 5,000,000. "2.5%" is 0.025, not 25%.
#ASSERT 2.5% EQUALS 0.025
#ASSERT `Article 13.8 — the fund management fee for a year on an account value of` 200_000_000 `at a rate of` (2.5%) EQUALS 5_000_000

-- 13.9 a: the rate on an instalment against the table. The same 90/70/40/0 by policy year
-- whatever the frequency: annual 1 = half-yearly 2 = quarterly 4 = monthly 12.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      f IS A `A premium frequency`
      r IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A regular basic premium instalment`
`instalment` n `paid as` f `charged at` r MEANS
    `A regular basic premium instalment` WITH
        `instalment number`   IS n
        `frequency`           IS f
        `amount`              IS 1_000_000
        `initial charge rate` IS r

#ASSERT `Article 13.9(a) — the guaranteed maximum is kept by the initial charge rate on` (`instalment` 2 `paid as` `annual premiums` `charged at` 0.7)
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 13.9(a) — the guaranteed maximum is kept by the initial charge rate on` (`instalment` 2 `paid as` `annual premiums` `charged at` 0.71))
#ASSERT `Article 13.9(a) — the guaranteed maximum is kept by the initial charge rate on` (`instalment` 12 `paid as` `monthly premiums` `charged at` 0.9)
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 13.9(a) — the guaranteed maximum is kept by the initial charge rate on` (`instalment` 13 `paid as` `monthly premiums` `charged at` 0.9))
#ASSERT `the guaranteed maximum initial charge rate for instalment` 1 `paid as` `annual premiums` EQUALS `the guaranteed maximum initial charge rate for instalment` 2 `paid as` `half-yearly premiums`
#ASSERT `the guaranteed maximum initial charge rate for instalment` 4 `paid as` `quarterly premiums` EQUALS `the guaranteed maximum initial charge rate for instalment` 12 `paid as` `monthly premiums`
#ASSERT `the guaranteed maximum initial charge rate for instalment` 2 `paid as` `annual premiums` EQUALS `the guaranteed maximum initial charge rate for instalment` 13 `paid as` `monthly premiums`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the guaranteed maximum initial charge rate for instalment` 0 `paid as` `annual premiums` BECAUSE "the Article 13.9(a) table has no row for that instalment number"
-- 13.9 b: a top-up's initial charge must be nil.
#ASSERT `Article 13.9(b) — the guaranteed maximum is kept by the initial charge rate on` (`A top-up premium` WITH `date paid` IS YMD 2030 3 12, `amount` IS 1, `initial charge rate` IS 0)
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 13.9(b) — the guaranteed maximum is kept by the initial charge rate on` (`A top-up premium` WITH `date paid` IS YMD 2030 3 12, `amount` IS 1, `initial charge rate` IS 0.01))
-- 13.9 c and e: 100,000 may go to 115,000 in a year, not 115,001.
#ASSERT `Article 13.9(c) and (e) — a fee of` 115_000 `is within the guaranteed maximum, against` 100_000 `a year before`
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 13.9(c) and (e) — a fee of` 115_001 `is within the guaranteed maximum, against` 100_000 `a year before`)
-- 13.9 d: at most twice the standard mortality rate.
#ASSERT `Article 13.9(d) — a risk premium rate of` 0.002 `is within the guaranteed maximum, against a standard mortality rate of` 0.001
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 13.9(d) — a risk premium rate of` 0.0021 `is within the guaranteed maximum, against a standard mortality rate of` 0.001)
-- 13.9 f: the partial withdrawal fee at most the switching fee that year.
#ASSERT `Article 13.9(f) — a partial withdrawal fee of` 200_000 `is within the guaranteed maximum, against a switching fee that year of` 200_000
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 13.9(f) — a partial withdrawal fee of` 200_001 `is within the guaranteed maximum, against a switching fee that year of` 200_000)
-- 13.9 g and h: spread 5%, fee 2.5%; 5.1% or 2.6% is over.
#ASSERT `Article 13.9(g) and (h) — the guaranteed maxima are kept by the spread and the fund management fee in` `the charges`
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 13.9(g) and (h) — the guaranteed maxima are kept by the spread and the fund management fee in` (`The charges in the Policy Schedule` WITH `monthly policy fee` IS 50_000, `risk premium rate` IS 0.0002, `switching fee` IS 100_000, `partial withdrawal fee` IS 200_000, `bid-offer spread` IS 0.051, `fund management fee rate per year` IS 0.025))
#ASSERT NOT (`Article 13.9(g) and (h) — the guaranteed maxima are kept by the spread and the fund management fee in` (`The charges in the Policy Schedule` WITH `monthly policy fee` IS 50_000, `risk premium rate` IS 0.0002, `switching fee` IS 100_000, `partial withdrawal fee` IS 200_000, `bid-offer spread` IS 0.05, `fund management fee rate per year` IS 0.026))

-- The table, every row at both edges (an open row at its first instalment and twelve on),
-- generated from source lines 619-662 by tools/gen_tables.py charge-tests.
#ASSERT `the guaranteed maximum initial charge rate for instalment` 1 `paid as` `annual premiums` EQUALS 90%   -- src:622-623
#ASSERT `the guaranteed maximum initial charge rate for instalment` 2 `paid as` `annual premiums` EQUALS 70%   -- src:624-625
